.\"
.\"	@(#)uname.2	8/1/92
.\"
.TH UNAME 2P "August 1, 1992"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
uname \-  (POSIX only)get system name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.ft B
#include <sys/utsname.h>
.PP
.ft B
int uname(struct utsname *\fIname\fP);
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The information in this specification applies
only to POSIX applications.
.PP
.I Uname
stores information identifying the current operating system
in the structure pointed to by 
.I name.
.PP
The structure 
.I utsname 
is defined in the header 
.I <sys/utsname.h> 
and contains the following members:
.PP
.nf
.RS
.DT
char	sysname[32] 
char	nodename[32]
char 	release[32]
char 	version[32]
char	machine[32]
.RE
.fi
.PP
.I Sysname
is set to the value ``NEXTSTEP''.
.I Nodename
is the hostname set by 
.IR hostname (1)
or
.IR sethostname (2).
.I Release
and 
.I version
reflects the level of the operating system.
.I Machine
identifies the hardware architecture.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
If successful
.I uname
returns a nonnegative value.  If
the request failed, \-1 is returned.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
hostname(1), 
sethostname(2)
